{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Last month, I chased cherry blossoms to Japan—and found so much more.\n\nI arrived in Kyoto just as the sakura began to unfurl, pink petals drifting like confetti over the Kamo River. I sat beneath a centuries-old tree, sipping matcha from a ceramic cup, listening to the rustle of leaves and distant temple bells. No phone, no plan—just stillness.\n\nTokyo was a whirlwind of neon and quiet corners. In Shibuya, I got lost in the scramble crossing, swept up in a tide of suits and sneakers. But an hour later, I found myself in a tiny alley in Shimokitazawa, sipping black coffee from a café run by a man who spoke no English—and didn’t need to. We smiled. He handed me a warm daifuku. I nodded. That was enough.\n\nI ate ramen at 2 a.m. in Fukuoka, slurping noodles so hot they made my eyes water. I bowed deeply to a shrine keeper who smiled and handed me a wooden omamori. I rode the Shinkansen, watching rice fields blur into mountains, feeling the quiet hum of a train that never rushed but always arrived.\n\nIn Hiroshima, I visited the Peace Memorial Park. The silence there was heavier than any sound. A single origami crane sat on the memorial bench—left by someone, maybe years ago. I added mine.\n\nJapan doesn’t shout. It whispers: in the rustle of a bamboo grove, the precision of a tea ceremony, the way a stranger bows before handing you a receipt.\n\nI came for the cherry blossoms. I left with a quieter heart.\n\n— 298 words", "logprobs": [{"token": "Last", "logprob": -1.208087682723999}, {"token": " month", "logprob": -0.018090255558490753}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -7.152531907195225e-06}, {"token": " I", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " chased", "logprob": -2.0831565856933594}, {"token": " cherry", "logprob": -0.004060002509504557}, {"token": " bloss", "logprob": -0.0001230164198204875}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token":